{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>You shall not eat any abomination.</b> It warns concerning the prohibition of forbidden foods, for it is a fence of holiness, as he has mentioned, for it is a holy people — for it is holy in mouth and in deed. And the Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: ״לא תאכל כל תועבה״ — anything I have abominated for you, you may not eat; for example, meat cooked in milk — this is something I have abominated for you, and it falls under ״you shall not eat.\""], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:48:13.006325218Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}